# Claim: a walk of a taken Map of Close values owns each entry it binds, so each value closes exactly once: at the step's end, through `close` in the body, at `next`, `break` or `return`, or, for the entries the walk left, when the walk ends. The checked heap traps a second end, on o0, o1 and o2.
# Hand-derived: keys walk in order a, b, c, d; "wc" closes in the body before its step line; the entries a `break` or `return` leaves close as the walk ends, in key order like any Map close (a break after the first entry closes the other three a to d); the borrowed walk closes all four when its Map ends.
fixture: taken_map_walk_closes_each_value_once.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet run --checked-alloc --optimize=none main.jet
exit: 0 # o0
stdout: = taken_map_walk_closes_each_value_once.out # o0
step: jet run --checked-alloc --optimize=basic main.jet
exit: 0 # o1
stdout: = taken_map_walk_closes_each_value_once.out # o1
step: jet run --checked-alloc --optimize=full main.jet
exit: 0 # o2
stdout: = taken_map_walk_closes_each_value_once.out # o2
